      "doctor_question": "Do you have trouble falling asleep?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Falling asleep? No, not really. I usually just hit the pillow and I'm out. Though, to be honest, half the time lately I end up falling asleep in my recliner. It's one of those big oversized leather ones, you know? I got it on sale at this furniture liquidation place a few years back. Best purchase I ever made. My wife hates it, she says it takes up way too much room in the den, but it used to have this really great massage feature. \n\nWell, the motor for it burned out a couple of months ago, actually. I flipped the whole chair over to try and fix it, but the wiring in those things is just a complete mess. It's not like the old Chevy engines where everything makes sense and you can actually trace the lines. I spent three hours just poking at the circuit board before I finally gave up... wait, what was the question? Oh, right, sleep. Yeah, no, my sleep is fine.",
