    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you find yourself falling asleep during the day when you don’t mean to?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "During the day? No, no, I don't really doze off like that. I'm usually too keyed up anyway. Plus, at work, it's just back-to-back calls. You wouldn't believe how angry people get over a five-dollar late fee on their account. Just Tuesday, I had this guy yelling at me for twenty minutes straight because he forgot to mail his check. He kept blaming the post office, which, you know, fair enough, the post office around my neighborhood has been pretty terrible lately. \n\nMy regular mail carrier, Frank, he's retiring next month, and the new guy filling in keeps putting my neighbor's mail in my box. They get these really high-end woodworking catalogs. Man, some of the lathes they sell in there are just incredible. I’ve always thought about getting into wood turning, making bowls or table legs, something like that. Seems like it would be a good way to keep my hands busy... but anyway, what did you ask? Oh, right, sleeping during the day. No, I stay awake just fine.",
