    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel restless or have trouble sitting still?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Well, yeah, I do. Especially if I have to sit through something slow, like a training video at work or a long appointment. I start feeling real boxed in, you know? Like I just have to stand up, stretch my legs, or at least do something with my hands. \n\nIt reminds me of this one training seminar they sent us to last year. Whole day thing at this hotel downtown. The chairs were those awful stacking banquet chairs, no padding at all. And the guy presenting, I swear he had the most monotone voice I’ve ever heard. He sounded exactly like my old high school history teacher, Mr. Henderson. Henderson used to just read straight from the textbook for an hour straight. I spent most of his class doodling in the margins of my notebook or taking my pen apart and putting it back together. I got so good at it I could reassemble a click pen blindfolded. Honestly, I think that's why I like fixing things so much, just figuring out how all the little pieces fit together. \n\nAnyway, during that seminar, I must have gotten up to get coffee like six times just to have an excuse to walk around. The coffee was terrible, too—tasted like burnt rubber. I ended up sneaking out at lunch and walking three blocks to find a decent diner. Found this great little place that made a killer pastrami on rye... wait, sorry, what were we talking about? Oh, right, sitting still. Yeah, it's tough for me. I just get this urge to move.",
