      "targeted_symptom": "functional_impairment",
      "patient_response": "Work? Yeah, it's actually starting to become a bit of a problem there. My supervisors have been bringing it up in my recent reviews. They keep pointing out that I have all these unfinished tickets, or I make these little mistakes that end up slowing the whole team down. It's frustrating because I really am trying hard, and I usually get along great with the customers. \n\nLike I was saying before about that guy with the late fee, I actually managed to calm him down eventually. We ended up talking about his grandson's little league team for a good ten minutes. I used to coach little league, you know, back when my son was younger. We had this one kid on the team, Tommy, who couldn't hit a ball to save his life, but man, he could run like the wind. Once he got on base, it was a guaranteed run. We made it all the way to the regional championships that year. We played this team from two towns over, and they had uniforms that looked just like the Oakland A's. I always liked those colors, the green and gold. Reminds me of this old jacket I used to have... wait, what was the question? Oh, right, problems. Yeah, at work it's definitely showing up in my reviews with the unfinished tickets and all that.",
