    {
      "turn": 6,
      "doctor_question": "Did these attention and focus problems start when you were a child?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Childhood? Yeah, actually. Looking back, this was around long before this job change. I know because my mom used to keep all my old report cards in this big cedar chest at the foot of her bed. Man, I love the smell of cedar. I actually bought a bunch of cedar blocks for my own closet a couple of months ago because I found a moth hole in my favorite wool sweater. It was this really nice navy blue cardigan, super warm. I tried to patch the hole myself, but my sewing skills are pretty much nonexistent. I ended up making this huge, lumpy knot on the sleeve, and my wife just took one look at it and laughed. I think she ended up donating it. I always wonder if whoever bought it at the thrift store managed to fix the sleeve or if they just wear it lumpy. \n\nBut anyway... what was I saying? Oh, right, the report cards in the chest. Yeah, I was looking through them a while back, and in grade school, pretty much all my teachers wrote the exact same thing in the comments section. They'd say that I was bright but careless, that I always talked out of turn, and that I constantly had to be reminded to stay with my work. So yeah, I guess I've been like this since I was a little kid.",
